Add, list, show, remove and reorder the access rules of a bucket

Usage:
  nexoctl access rule [flags]
  nexoctl access rule [command]

Available Commands:
  add         Add an access rule to a bucket
  info        Show an access rule
  list        List the access rules of a bucket, in evaluation order
  move        Change the priority of an access rule
  remove      Remove an access rule

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for rule

Global Flags:
      --config-dir string   configuration directory (default $NEXOCTL_CONFIG_DIR or ~/.nexoctl)
      --debug               dump the HTTP requests and responses on stderr, with the secrets redacted
      --json                print JSON Lines (one object per line with a "status" member)
      --no-color            disable colors (also with the NO_COLOR environment variable)
  -q, --quiet               hide confirmations and progress (results and errors are still printed)

Use "nexoctl access rule [command] --help" for more information about a command.
